y lines in 2007's one more day peter  parker and mary jane watson parker make  a deal with the demonic mephisto to  erase their marriage from existence in  exchange for saving aunt may's life in  the 2010 sequel story one moment in time  peter asked dr strange to erase the  public's knowledge of a secret identity  given the fallout of his and mary jane's  agreement with the demon and after some  convincing the sorcerer supreme agrees  for what it's worth it doesn't seem like  the no way home filmmakers are unaware  of these parallels there's even a  protest sign in the trailer of tom  holland's peter parker with devil horns  and the words devil in disguise scrawled  underneath his photo which feels like a  reference to the role that mephisto  plays in the one more day comic  early on in the spider-man no way home  trailer peter parker is interrogated by  the authorities over his alleged  involvement in the death of mysterio at  first glance the scene doesn't seem  particularly noteworthy though there's  been some speculation about a particular  lawyer what we know for sure though is  that those aren't just any government  officials as a matter of fact they're  damage control agents as revealed by a  jacket worn by one of the agents the  organization originally founded by  shield and later turned into a joint  venture between stark industries and the  us government specializes in cleaning up  the destruction caused by superhero  battles and in the maintenance of all  weapons and artifacts left over from the  scenes of said battles damage control is  notably the same organization that sends  adrian tombs down his path of villainy  in 2017's spider-man homecoming  he's right i overextended myself  while the organization's involvement in  spider-man no way home doesn't reveal  anything new about the movie's plot that  we didn't already know it's a fun easter  egg for marvel cinematic universe fans  and acts as just yet another link  between no way home and the previous 